---
title: "Export images and media"
sidebar:
  order: 10
---

Export photographs on their own, either one file at a time or as a single archive.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Open a media item and select `Export` for one file, or open the media gallery, turn on selection, and select `Export` for several.
2. Choose the image format. `Original` copies the file unchanged, and JPEG, PNG, or WebP converts it.
3. Resize when the files are larger than you need, using the width and height fields for one image or the maximum longer side for a selection.
4. Adjust JPEG quality if you chose JPEG. The default of 85 percent suits most reports.
5. For a selection, choose TAR.GZ for a smaller archive, which macOS, Linux, and Windows 11 open natively, or ZIP when the file is going to an older Windows machine.
6. Set the file name and destination, select `Export`, and check the exported and skipped counts.
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
A large selection can take several minutes while it converts. Keep NAHPU open until the progress panel finishes.
{% /aside %}

